  "text": "So here's the idea the whole project hangs on. Don't retrain the big model at all. You take a large, pre-trained model that already has a lot of general visual and spatial understanding built in think of it as a brain and you freeze it. You never touch it again. Instead, you bolt on these little add-ons we call adapters. Each one is tiny a fraction of a percent of that brain and each one teaches it exactly ONE thing: this is what an apartment layout is; this is what an architectural programme is; this is what makes a layout efficient. They're small, so each one is quick and cheap to train. They're modular one skill apiece. And they combine you just stack the ones a project needs. Stack the right adapters, and a general-purpose model turns into an architect for timber extensions.",
